['Communities, security and policy','Standard/extended/large communities have distinct encoding and applications. send-community behavior and receiving route maps determine whether a tag produces action. Origin validation checks authorized origin/max-length, not every route leak. Export relationship controls, prefix limits and intentional import filters address other risks. FlowSpec actions require trusted origin and bounded validation.'],
['PIC, graceful restart and protection','PIC can preprogram alternate forwarding to reduce per-prefix work on failure; support/topology matter. Graceful restart retains routes during a control restart based on negotiated behavior and timers; stale paths can harm forwarding if the assumption is wrong. LLGR extends retention under supported policy. CoPP protects device processing but must preserve legitimate routing/control traffic. Detection, alternate activation and final convergence are separate measurements.']
